  "fidelityReview": {
    "target": "medium-fi",
    "status": "passed",
    "notes": "Complete original medium-fi greenhouse exterior: log base on pale plinth, genuinely transparent gable panes and glazed end, timber rafters/purlins, two opening roof lights, boarded entry/fuel bay with open wooden door, coarse split-log alcove, opposite-end pale chimney and supported threshold. Simple inner benches are reconstructed for the clear-roof view. Reuse existing wood_log, wood_plain, wood_vertical, plaster_lime and stone_limestone graphs plus a texture-free clear-glass material; no private atlas, copied photograph pixels, flowers, trees or people baked into the building. Photo-led one-story scale: low log body1.25m above floor, glazed gable ridge3.15m, chimney4.12m, timber entry/fuel bay2.2m long, real .88x1.95m doorway with leaf open90degrees. Floor 0.7182087492670064m above outside datum; original corner grades 0.568/0.230/0.165/0.465m. Floor is.15m above highest sampled corner; small plinth/foundation follows the standard terrain. Bay widths, roof pitch, vent positions, fuel census and inner benches remain reconstructed. The mapped greenhouse name/type and footprint support identity/scale. Exact historic roof pitch, chimney/threshold heights, end-bay orientation, vent count/placement, hidden benches/floor, fuel census and glazing schedule remain photo-led approximations. The glass is a simple browser PBR approximation, not physical refraction. Estate service inventory remains incomplete."
